  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Afghanistan Joint Response 2024-26 - Joint Budget</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Afghanistan faces a large humanitarian crisis, with high levels of food insecurity, and limited access to basic services. After the takeover by the DFA, although generally access has improved, services have reduced and restrictions on women are increasing daily. Based on the high needs, Afghanistan was selected as part of the DRA Joint Responses for 2024-2026.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Most vulnerable food insecure households, with focus on vulnerable female and  child headed households, households with PWD, elderly or chronically ill.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">alleviate suffering and increasing access to basic services, and reducing negative coping strategies of most vunerable, food insecure people in Kandahar (incl Zabul), Nangarhar and Herat.</narrative>
  </description>
